---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="About & independence"
  description="Who runs YEGFacts, what he thinks about Edmonton, and why the method is built so that it does not matter."
>
  <header class="border-b border-rule pb-6">
    <h1 class="text-[1.75rem] leading-[1.15] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.022em] sm:text-display">
      About
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
      YEGFacts checks claims about Edmonton civic government against public records, data and
      research, and publishes what it finds with the evidence attached.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="mt-10 max-w-prose space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.015em] text-forest">Who runs it</h2>
    <p>
      YEGFacts is built and operated by <strong class="font-semibold">Ildar Abdulin</strong>, in
      Edmonton. One person, working in bursts, on evenings and weekends. There is no newsroom behind
      this and no institution funding it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reach me at{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="text-navy underline">{SITE.email}</a>. Everything
      the site is made of — content, prompts, scripts, edit history — is public at{' '}
      <a href={SITE.repo} rel="noopener" class="text-navy underline">github.com/civicfacts/yegfacts</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-prose space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.015em] text-forest">
      What I think, and why it doesn't decide anything here
    </h2>
    <p>
      I have views about urban policy. I think density and transit are usually good for a city, and
      I am more interested in what a policy produced than in who proposed it. Pretending otherwise
      would be the dishonest move, so: that is where I start from.
    </p>
    <p>
      The method is built so those views do not get to pick the answers. Three models research each
      claim independently, without seeing each other's work. The canonical finding is computed from
      their verdicts by a rule written down in advance and published, not chosen after the fact. My
      role is applying that published methodology — freezing the brief before the models run,
      holding the publication gate, and editing prose. Since methodology v1.1 the gate itself runs
      as a dedicated AI audit under a standing delegation from me: it checks every published
      statement against the archived bytes of its sources and release-checks the raw artifacts. I
      remain accountable for everything published and can revert any of it.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is not a promise that I have no influence; it is a structure that makes influence
      visible. Every finding on this site shows the evidence it rests on, what each model concluded
      including where they disagreed, and a dated history of every revision. If I ever overrode the
      process, the override would be inspectable in the version-controlled history, sitting next to
      the evidence it contradicted.
    </p>
    <p>
      A test of whether this is working: the findings should cut in more than one political
      direction. If every conclusion here flattered the same side, you should stop trusting it —
      and so should I.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-prose space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.015em] text-forest">Interests to declare</h2>
    <p>
      I hold no office and am not a member of any political party. I have no contract with the City
      of Edmonton and no financial interest in any of the programs checked here. If that changes, it
      gets written on this page before it affects anything published.
    </p>
    <p>
      YEGFacts is not a charity and does not solicit charitable donations. If contributions are ever
      accepted to cover research and operating costs, they are disclosed and carry no editorial
      influence — see the <a href="/support" class="text-navy underline">support page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12 max-w-prose space-y-4 text-[1.0625rem] leading-relaxed">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.015em] text-forest">Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If something here is wrong, the fastest fix is to point at the evidence. Corrections are
      published as dated entries in the article history on the page that was wrong — nothing is
      quietly edited.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href={`${SITE.repo}/issues/new`} rel="noopener" class="text-navy underline">
        Open an issue
      </a>{' '}
      or <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="text-navy underline">email me</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
